'''''Leskea polycarpa'',''' commonly known as '''many-fruited leskea,'''<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Leskea polycarpa |url=https://www.britishbryologicalsociety.org.uk/learning/species-finder/leskea-polycarpa/ |access-date=2025-03-25 |website=British Bryological Society |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref name="GBIF" /> is a species of [[moss]] belonging to the family [[Leskeaceae]].<ref name="worldfloraonline.org">{{cite web |title=Leskea polycarpa Ehrh. ex Hedw. |url=http://www.worldfloraonline.org/taxon/wfo-0001163007 |website=www.worldfloraonline.org |access-date=5 February 2021}}</ref>

It is native to Eurasia and North America,<ref name="GBIF">{{cite web |title=Leskea polycarpa Ehrhart ex Hedwig, 1801 |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/2681370 |website=www.gbif.org |access-date=5 February 2021 |language=en}}</ref> usually found on the trunks and branches of trees near bodies of water, but also growing in dryer areas.<ref name=":0" /><ref>Leskea polycarpa pdf.https://www.britishbryologicalsociety.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/Leskea-polycarpa.pdf<nowiki/>Retrieved 25 March 2025''.''</ref> 

== Description ==
''Leskea polycarpa'' has creeping stems with spreading branches.<ref name="worldfloraonline.org" /> The '''leaves''' on the stem are longer than wide, about 0.8–1.6 mm (0.031–0.063 inches) long, while the branch leaves are about 0.5–0.8 mm (0.02–0.031 inches) in length and are [[Ovate (botany)|ovate]] to [[lanceolate]] in shape.<ref name="worldfloraonline.org" /> The '''[[spore]] capsules''', 2–3 mm (0.079–0.118 inches) long, are brown to yellowish in colour, curved in shape;<ref name="worldfloraonline.org" /> the [[seta#Plant setae|'''seta''']] (capsule stalk) is 7–12 mm (0.28–0.47 inches) long and can be red to brownish-orange.<ref name="worldfloraonline.org" />
